WEBVTT

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:06.930
Hey, did you ever hear about that dealer?

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:08.030
It hurts...

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.470
Yeah.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:09.980
It hurts...

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:12.600
It's bitter...

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:20.040
Nico!

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:22.790
He's dead, huh?

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:26.410
He's got two personalities,
so they call him...

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:29.160
Nico.

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:34.180
Hello.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.680
Holy shit...

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:38.850
This is bad news!

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.180
This is really bad!

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:44.950
Uh, you keep saying that, but...

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:47.780
I have no idea what's so bad!

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.570
Explain!

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:52.720
When the medicine wears off, 
Nico goes out of control.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:58.340
Normally, humans subconsciously
limit their abilities.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.060
But due to side effects from some 
experiments they did a long time ago,

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:05.760
the functions of the brain that control that

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.460
are more fragile in Nico than in most.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:08.900
I see.

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:12.790
So Okina's medicine helps control them.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:15.450
And when it wears off...

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.150
That's bad news!

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:19.050
See? I told you!

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.670
Stop this stupid conversation.

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:25.850
I may be stupid, but I'm still hot!

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:27.410
That's right!

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:29.590
Don't sigh!

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.230
Hey!

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:32.960
I have to save Nico.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:36.630
Okina said that going out of control

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:38.040
could destroy Nico's body.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:38.930
You can't!

00:01:38.930 --> 00:01:40.900
There are monsters everywhere.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:41.740
But...

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:45.620
We have to go forward.

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:48.380
Nico...

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:51.500
What is this guy?

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:55.380
He just... changed all of a sudden.

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:01.890
Smells good!

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:08.390
I smell the medicine on you, you, you!

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:13.450
The medicine is my lifeline.

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:15.940
If you don't want to die,

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:18.990
give it to me!

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:41.490
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:51.000
<b>Awakening Poison</b>

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:51.250
Medicine! Medicine! Medicine!

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:57.630
What is he talking about?

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:02.130
Medicine... Medicine...

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:05.140
Finish him off!

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:11.660
Watch out!

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:19.320
No... No!

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.820
This is not what I want!

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:26.200
This won't end Nico's pain!

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:28.160
What?!

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:35.080
Nasty fireworks!

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:40.480
You've gotta be kidding me...

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:44.440
Why are Hachiman and Number 25
from Building 13 fighting?

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:46.050
I didn't believe it at first, but...

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:48.420
His symptoms are really that bad?

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:49.730
What do I do?

00:04:49.730 --> 00:04:51.700
Should I go out now?

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:56.310
You must think this is a joke...

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:58.770
But it's over now.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:03.010
He's gone?

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:06.660
Up here!

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:05.640
What?!

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:13.270
Get off me!

00:05:13.270 --> 00:05:14.910
Do it, Rokuriki!

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.290
I won't let you!

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:19.090
What?!

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:19.790
Upa!

00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:23.420
Right, right. Hold him tight, okay?

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:25.100
It's been a while,

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:27.930
so I don't know if my first try will succeed.

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:33.270
Good.

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:36.190
Damn it! He burned up the talisman?

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:37.440
Damn!

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:41.270
I've had enough of you!

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.160
Medicine...

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:51.660
So this is the sample I've heard about?

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:55.830
He's the only one who 
survived using the stuff.

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:00.170
It hurts...

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:02.570
There are barely any aftereffects,

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:05.210
and after a week, his body becomes normal.

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:08.340
So it's possible to recycle them?

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:09.590
Interesting!

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:16.670
We're going to try a new 
drug we just got in today...

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:18.690
Using you.

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:21.690
Medicine... Medicine..

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:24.700
Don't worry. It'll be fine.

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:27.000
Medicine is good for you.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:33.490
<i>I can't tell how he's going to move!</i>

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:37.500
<i>No, I can't tell if the way 
he's moving is even human!</i>

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:43.290
What the hell are you?!

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:46.260
I told you, he's poison.

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:51.280
It's possible for humans to break this badly.

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:57.390
Their human behaviors, language, 
responses, limits, all of it breaks...

00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:59.180
And they go out of control.

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:07.230
What you were once trying to do 
was make more people like this.

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:10.600
Make me more!

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:13.160
This'll be worth a fortune!

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:16.870
I can't stop laughing!

00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:21.350
Qi, you're the hen that 
lays the golden eggs!

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:26.930
Do you understand what that medicine is now?

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:28.090
You bastard...

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:30.180
Why did you come here?

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:32.970
If you're just here to watch, I'll kill you.

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:35.200
What are you talking about?

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:37.120
I'm here to work.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:39.750
I'll handle him.

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:42.060
Medicine!

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:44.560
Looks like he can tell 
instantly by the smell.

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:48.920
It's one unexpected thing after another.

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:51.650
This is just about the only way...

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:59.240
Calm down!

00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:05.160
Whoa...

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:12.020
What did you inject him with?

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:13.100
Nothing special.

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:16.550
I just used the same medicine he always uses.

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:20.690
Well, I did adjust it to make it work quicker.

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:25.030
It'll be a lot easier now 
that he's out of the way.

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:29.000
They're all that's left now.

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:32.190
That's right.

00:08:34.970 --> 00:08:36.200
Do it.

00:08:39.650 --> 00:08:41.680
What?

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:48.230
You bastard! What's the idea?!

00:08:48.230 --> 00:08:52.170
You should know exactly what the idea is.

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:55.050
This is the kind of guy I am.

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:58.790
I injected you with a special 
medicine made just for you.

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:03.390
Soon your brain and nerves 
will be paralyzed and useless.

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:06.070
Was this your plan from the start?

00:09:06.070 --> 00:09:09.720
You were planning to kill me 
from the start too, weren't you?

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:13.400
So I just took care of you first.

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:15.210
Hachiman,

00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:18.030
you've got a good eye for 
judging people, sure.

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:21.750
And you're better at threatening 
and making trades than me.

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:24.720
But that's what did you in.

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:29.700
You won't immediately kill 
people you think you can use.

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:33.720
You use them for all they're 
worth and then crush them.

00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:36.140
People who hate losing more than anything else

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:39.320
can't make quick judgments.

00:09:41.050 --> 00:09:44.720
Well, if you were still 
trying to use a guy like me,

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:46.970
in a sense, you're a nice guy.

00:09:46.970 --> 00:09:51.290
But I'll never forgive you.

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:54.230
Not you. Not ever.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:57.200
You really sold it?

00:09:57.430 --> 00:09:58.990
I didn't have a choice.

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:00.700
It was the boss's orders.

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:03.450
But he's just a kid!

00:10:03.650 --> 00:10:05.610
It has to be this kid.

00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:07.080
Why?

00:10:07.260 --> 00:10:09.870
Even among the clan of qigong users,

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:12.010
his talents surpass any of the others.

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:14.980
Enough so that he's worshiped 
as something special.

00:10:16.660 --> 00:10:21.180
The boss, and that organ 
collector, realized that.

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:26.390
The organs of a top-rank qigong user 
aren't something you can get easily.

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:30.350
Wait... Is that why you kidnapped him?

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:34.400
They apparently told the clan that he'd died.

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:43.910
No, I'll never forgive you.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:49.090
I will defeat you!

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:55.000
<b>Nanbaka</b>

00:10:58.270 --> 00:10:59.250
You...

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:02.590
You traitor!

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:09.690
Die!

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:14.130
Ow...

00:11:18.570 --> 00:11:22.450
Oh, my... It's been a while, huh?

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:24.840
No, it hasn't.

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:27.240
You've been here the whole time, right?

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:29.350
Sorry.

00:11:29.350 --> 00:11:33.410
What the hell were you thinking, 
giving Hachiman the medicine?

00:11:33.410 --> 00:11:35.690
No, see... Well...

00:11:35.690 --> 00:11:38.340
Um... sorry.

00:11:38.570 --> 00:11:41.540
If "sorry" was enough, 
we wouldn't need prisons.

00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:43.970
Don't look at me the way you look at garbage!

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:46.550
Um... You know what they say, right?

00:11:46.550 --> 00:11:49.000
To deceive your enemies, 
you must first... something.

00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:51.950
I'm sorry I didn't say anything,

00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:54.690
but I brought the keys to 
the cell and handcuffs...

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:56.090
We don't need those now.

00:11:56.090 --> 00:11:57.200
It's too late.

00:11:57.200 --> 00:11:59.290
We're past that point now.

00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:01.110
At least give me some praise!

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:06.180
Anyway, I'm glad both you guys 
and Number 25 are okay.

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:10.490
Why are you pretending to 
be a good guy now, you scum?

00:12:10.490 --> 00:12:12.170
Whoa, that's harsh!

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:15.750
Why did you do all this without telling us?

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:19.500
Because you're both the type to 
act before you speak, right?

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:22.120
If you knew what was going on here,

00:12:22.120 --> 00:12:25.140
I figured you'd take action somehow.

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:28.470
And it was Enki who escaped.

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:31.770
One wrong move and you 
might have been killed.

00:12:32.970 --> 00:12:36.320
I don't want to make such a risky wager.

00:12:37.050 --> 00:12:40.030
You've gotta at least take care of yourself.

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:43.780
You're starting over now, after all.

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:45.130
Qi...

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:49.160
Unlike me, you guys are still...

00:12:49.890 --> 00:12:52.160
You never even do anything!

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:56.170
Why is it only at times like these 
that you do stuff without telling us?!

00:12:56.830 --> 00:12:59.220
It was the same on the day 
you betrayed Hachiman.

00:12:59.220 --> 00:13:02.590
Did you think you could 
do anything by yourself?

00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:03.640
Upa...

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:06.050
Don't you tell me to take care of myself.

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:07.900
You don't have the right to say that!

00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:12.400
He's a strong kid.

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:15.690
He's had organs stolen, and he's lost his home.

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:19.960
But even so, he's obeying the boss 
and trying to buy back his organs.

00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:23.570
And that's why he's doing 
this underground work?

00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:27.360
But that's impossible.

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:31.580
Before he can do it, I know he'll...

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:42.100
Hey, can you do me a favor?

00:13:44.860 --> 00:13:48.340
Give him my organs.

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:53.090
Nobody asked you to do that.

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:56.100
You only ever think about yourself.

00:14:00.350 --> 00:14:01.760
Master!

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:03.440
I have to save Master!

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:05.320
Master!

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:07.580
Master?

00:14:08.070 --> 00:14:09.610
At this point...

00:14:09.610 --> 00:14:14.830
I don't even know why I'm training!

00:14:15.150 --> 00:14:19.710
I don't need your help, you scum!

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:23.150
You're as harsh as ever, huh?

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:26.520
This cell is important to me, too.

00:14:26.520 --> 00:14:30.430
We need this place if 
we're going to start over.

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:35.890
To start over...

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:42.630
I lost again!

00:14:42.630 --> 00:14:44.400
Rock, you suck at this.

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:46.280
Jyugo's gonna start beating you at this rate!

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:47.490
Jyugo?!

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:49.540
Ugh, anything but that!

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:51.950
What's that supposed to mean?

00:14:52.960 --> 00:14:54.890
Okay, one more round!

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:57.340
Nico, come join us.

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:01.040
Okay!

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:04.600
It's because I came here and met everyone

00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:06.920
that I was able to smile again.

00:15:09.570 --> 00:15:12.100
I'm sure we can all start over.

00:15:13.020 --> 00:15:15.610
You were lucky to get the chance.

00:15:19.150 --> 00:15:21.960
I can't just look away.

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:25.020
You're making me laugh.

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:30.130
"Start over," my ass.

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:32.030
"A chance," my ass!

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:35.280
You idiots are beyond salvation!

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:39.540
You don't have any chance at all, traitors!

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:43.570
The guards are traitors, 
and the prisoners, too.

00:15:43.570 --> 00:15:46.310
You're even betraying my expectations.

00:15:46.310 --> 00:15:50.300
"The Traitorous Building 5"
is the perfect name for you!

00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:53.430
Every single one of you...

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:57.310
You're all weak, but you've got 
the guts to try and bite at me!

00:15:59.310 --> 00:16:00.290
Huh?

00:16:00.970 --> 00:16:02.560
What did you say?

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:04.940
Who are you calling weak?

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:08.440
I dare you to say that again, pig.

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:12.070
Do you really think you can defeat me?

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:16.320
I guess, as big as he is, it won't 
take effect immediately, huh?

00:16:16.320 --> 00:16:18.950
Maybe I should've made it stronger.

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:21.480
You're always too optimistic.

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:23.420
That's how you screw up your plans.

00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:25.460
I'll help you a little.

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:28.340
If we're going to do it, 
I want to go all the way.

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:30.420
What are you babbling about?

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:33.340
I'm counting on you.

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:36.010
Both of you!

00:16:37.360 --> 00:16:38.520
Whoops!

00:16:39.650 --> 00:16:41.620
What are you aiming at?

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:45.160
You can't honestly expect those 
things to work at this point!

00:16:59.070 --> 00:17:00.320
Hey, now...

00:17:00.320 --> 00:17:02.470
Such messy attacks!

00:17:04.820 --> 00:17:07.710
Weren't you going to defeat me?

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:09.590
You're not even grazing me!

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:12.490
No, this is more than enough.

00:17:15.560 --> 00:17:16.590
Huh?

00:17:16.590 --> 00:17:17.490
What are you—

00:17:17.490 --> 00:17:20.070
Just as there are different 
types of medicines and poisons,

00:17:20.070 --> 00:17:22.790
there are lots of ways to use them.

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:26.000
What are you talking—

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:29.560
Wh-What?

00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:32.330
You don't need a wound to inject the poison.

00:17:32.330 --> 00:17:34.570
There are easier ways.

00:17:34.750 --> 00:17:35.990
For example,

00:17:37.170 --> 00:17:39.510
turning it into a gas and making you inhale it.

00:17:39.510 --> 00:17:41.450
Y-You bastard...

00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:44.540
This is a special medicine 
I made just for you.

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:46.290
As much as you've moved around,

00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:48.020
it'll work quickly.

00:17:49.760 --> 00:17:53.460
It's a strong medicine that 
even I don't use often.

00:17:53.660 --> 00:17:56.280
But I decided I wouldn't forgive you,

00:17:56.280 --> 00:17:57.470
so it's okay, right?

00:18:01.440 --> 00:18:02.670
What is this place?

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:05.120
Not bad, huh?

00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:08.850
Wow... There's a place like this in Building 5?

00:18:09.010 --> 00:18:11.060
It's not done yet,

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:14.360
but it's going to be the
courtyard for Building 5.

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:16.070
The courtyard for Building 5...

00:18:16.690 --> 00:18:20.120
And why'd you bring me here?

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:24.430
I once asked you about poisons, right?

00:18:24.430 --> 00:18:25.690
Yeah.

00:18:25.690 --> 00:18:29.500
Whether there was a poison that couldn't 
be detected in a body, right?

00:18:30.480 --> 00:18:32.100
Actually, yeah.

00:18:32.100 --> 00:18:36.010
A detective investigating a 
poisoning case asked me about it.

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:40.360
He said there should be a prisoner who 
knows about medicines and poisons.

00:18:40.360 --> 00:18:44.040
He did a lot of investigating 
and found your name.

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:48.900
Well, knowing your job,

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:50.960
and the fact that you came from the outside,

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:53.020
it makes sense, but...

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:55.030
Don't get so down.

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:57.210
The case was solved.

00:18:57.210 --> 00:18:58.780
I see.

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:02.870
It's because you were honest with me.

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:07.850
<i>No... It wasn't because I was honest.</i>

00:19:08.640 --> 00:19:11.610
<i>It's because you believed me.</i>

00:19:12.600 --> 00:19:14.180
No matter what else,

00:19:14.180 --> 00:19:18.300
you were needed because of your 
skills, knowledge, and experience.

00:19:18.610 --> 00:19:20.550
Isn't that great?

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:26.060
<i>Why does everyone call an 
honest guy like him a traitor?</i>

00:19:26.560 --> 00:19:31.440
Okay, so you brought me here to thank 
me for helping to solve the case?

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:33.000
Sure, think of it that way.

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:36.630
But I'm not allowed here at all, am I?

00:19:36.630 --> 00:19:38.250
Did you get permission?

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:43.450
Well, once this place is finished, 
you definitely won't be allowed in.

00:19:44.550 --> 00:19:47.080
Then wasn't it a risk to bring me here?

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:50.460
But it's not done yet, right?

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:53.440
<i>He did that to his own brother...</i>

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:57.630
<i>Is it that wrong to believe in him?</i>

00:19:58.740 --> 00:20:03.590
I don't want to doubt what he believes in.

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:06.970
Hachiman...

00:20:07.300 --> 00:20:09.350
I'm going to defeat you.

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:12.360
I'll defeat you, and then here,

00:20:13.180 --> 00:20:15.230
in our Building 5,

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:19.110
we'll start over.

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:21.310
What is this?

00:20:22.460 --> 00:20:24.490
I'm strangling myself?!

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:26.490
Alter the recipe a bit,

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:30.160
and you can control the brain, 
nerves, and muscles, you know.

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:35.900
And then, what happens when you give a 
certain signal... a certain stimulus?

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:38.380
Stop it! Please!

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:43.880
Have you ever spared someone who 
asked you for your help like that?

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:47.710
You should know this well.

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:50.930
Stop... Stop it!

00:20:50.930 --> 00:20:55.070
I don't kill people myself.

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:04.760
Did you kill him?

00:21:04.760 --> 00:21:07.560
No, I just knocked him out.

00:21:07.560 --> 00:21:09.770
The medicine's mostly taken effect.

00:21:09.770 --> 00:21:11.880
It would be dangerous to kill him.

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:15.870
You did it! You did it!

00:21:15.870 --> 00:21:17.350
You beat him!

00:21:17.350 --> 00:21:20.290
Are you feeling okay?

00:21:20.290 --> 00:21:22.410
Yeah, I'm okay.

00:21:22.410 --> 00:21:24.230
Looks like the medicine worked.

00:21:24.230 --> 00:21:25.880
Glad to hear it!

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:29.390
That was amazing, Master! Liang-kun!

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:33.020
Huh? Hey, Number 25? What about me?

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:36.210
I think I played a big part in this.

00:21:36.760 --> 00:21:37.520
Hop...

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:42.560
You can be really scary 
sometimes, huh, old man?

00:21:42.560 --> 00:21:45.150
I never thought I'd hear that from you.

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:48.900
And please don't call me an old man!

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:25.590 --> 00:23:28.290
We went back to search for Nico,

00:23:28.290 --> 00:23:30.420
and were caught up in a 
huge flood for some reason,

00:23:30.420 --> 00:23:32.470
then lured to the second underground floor.

00:23:32.470 --> 00:23:34.010
What is this water?

00:23:34.010 --> 00:23:36.810
And then a kappa showed up!

00:23:36.510 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Washed Away...</b>

00:23:36.810 --> 00:23:38.100
Next time: "Washed Away..."
